# == localization (must precede any string consumer) ==
core\locale\enUS.lua
# Non-enUS translations. Each chunk self-gates on GetLocale() (with the
# QUIDB.global.selectedLocale override) and returns immediately unless it is
# the active one, so only one table is ever built — the other nine cost compile
# time only, and their bytecode is collectable as soon as they return.
#
# They must be HERE, not in a LoadOnDemand addon: locale.lua (next) captures
# ns.LocaleData.active as an UPVALUE, so an overlay arriving later never
# reaches ns.L at all. File-scope consumers (BINDING_NAME_* in
# QUI_Bags/bags/bags.lua) and everything built during the login sequence
# read ns.L before any options addon could load.
#
# They used to be ten LoadOnDemand QUI_OptionsSearch_<loc> sub-addons, which
# cost 10 shipped folders to save ~51 ms of login compile.
core\locale\deDE.lua
core\locale\esES.lua
core\locale\esMX.lua
core\locale\frFR.lua
core\locale\itIT.lua
core\locale\koKR.lua
core\locale\ptBR.lua
core\locale\ruRU.lua
core\locale\zhCN.lua
core\locale\zhTW.lua
core\locale\locale.lua

